{"term":"fireman","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:891e2a84410e063b4a","definition":"Someone (especially male) who is skilled in the work of fighting fire.","example":"By February 1944 there were over two thousand women employed at the Alabama Dry Dock and Shipbuilding Company [...]. There were also female firemen on almost every shipyard crane [...].","pos":"noun","synonyms":["firefighter","smoke eater"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["firemanic","fireman's carry","firemanship"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireman#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2286ceb343cadd817a","definition":"A person (originally a man) who keeps the fire going underneath a steam boiler (originally, shoveling coal by hand), particularly on a railroad locomotive or steamship.","example":"He looked around his cab at his black greasy fireman, saying 'shovel on a little more coal, and when we cross that White Oak Mountain, you can watch Old 97 roll'.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["stoker","bakehead"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["firemanic","fireman's carry","firemanship"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireman#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec0666827cc4dca266","definition":"An assistant on any locomotive, whether steam-powered or not.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["firemanic","fireman's carry","firemanship"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireman#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:83059d5624cb7221c0","definition":"A relief pitcher (reflecting the figurative analogy of rescu